    "response": "\"  \n* Begin by holding the dog's leash and standing in front of it, facing it. Say \"Sit\" and wait for the dog to sit. Praise and reward the dog with a treat once it sits. Repeat this several times a day.  \n\n* Use a treat as a reward for the dog's attention. When the dog sits, give the treat and say \"Good job.\" Gradually increase the distance and time before giving the treat to build the dog's confidence.  \n\n* Practice the \"Stay\" command by standing in front of the dog and saying \"Stay.\" Wait for the dog to stay in place, then reward it with a treat. Once the dog understands, gradually increase the duration of the stay.  \n\"",
